  "verdict": "pended",
  "governing_rule": "MP-PAI-001",
  "reason": "The request meets basic eligibility, network, and diagnosis-code requirements, but the clinical documentation does not clearly satisfy the medical policy criteria for a lumbar transforaminal epidural steroid injection. Specifically: (1) conservative therapy adherence is described as inconsistent, which the policy states does not clearly satisfy the conservative management criterion; (2) the sensory examination is described as 'subjectively reduced' without a clear dermatomal pattern, which does not satisfy the dermatomal correlation criterion; and (3) the note itself states uncertainty as to whether the MRI finding at L5-S1 fully accounts for the reported symptom distribution, raising a question of imaging-clinical concordance. These ambiguities require additional clinical information before a coverage determination can be made.",
  "missing_information": [
    "Clarification of adherence to the home exercise/physical therapy program (duration and consistency)",
    "Detailed sensory examination specifying the exact dermatomal distribution of symptoms",
    "Physician attestation or additional clinical correlation confirming the MRI finding at L5-S1 corresponds to the reported right leg radicular pattern"
  ]
}
